  data: {
    LLM: "Dump your 'heavies' early. High doublendtiles (6-6, 5-5) are a massive liability in Gallinazo. If you can't play them early, they will balloon your score if the deal ends suddenly.\n\nPip Management: Toward the end of a deal, try to keep tiles that give you the most matching options (like a 1nd1 or 2nd2) rather than tiles with high pips. A low-value 'dead end' tile can be used to block the game if you are sure you have the lowest score.\n\nThe Block Trap: If you have a very low pip count (e.g., only a 0-1 and 1nd1 left), you may want to deliberately block the line. In Gallinazo, if you can block the game while holding the lowest count, you force every opponent to take a full point hit.",
    Player: "Dump your 'heavies' early. High doublendtiles (6-6, 5-5) are a massive liability in Gallinazo. If you can't play them early, they will balloon your score if the deal ends suddenly.\n\nPip Management: Toward the end of a deal, try to keep tiles that give you the most matching options (like a 1nd1 or 2nd2) rather than tiles with high pips. A low-value 'dead end' tile can be used to block the game if you are sure you have the lowest score.\n\nThe Block Trap: If you have a very low pip count (e.g., only a 0-1 and 1nd1 left), you may want to deliberately block the line. In Gallinazo, if you can block the game while holding the lowest count, you force every opponent to take a full point hit.",
